{
  "id": "calc.rbc-units-screen-compatibility",
  "slug": "rbc-units-screen-compatibility",
  "language": "en",
  "title": "RBC Units pour Screen pour Compatibility",
  "short_title": "Épreuves de compatibilité des globules rouges",
  "calc_type": "calculator",
  "purpose": [
    "Traitement",
    "Formule"
  ],
  "specialties": [
    "hematologie",
    "biologie"
  ],
  "diseases": [
    "Anémie"
  ],
  "chief_complaints": [
    "Saignement",
    "Faiblesse"
  ],
  "abbreviations": [
    "inventory screen",
    "antigen profile",
    "red blood cell",
    "APPROXIMATE NUMBER OF UNITS FOR COMPATIBILITY TESTING"
  ],
  "dosing": false,
  "formula": "x = number of units required / frequency of units negative for the antigen\n\nwhere x = minimum number of units to antigen type\n\nExample for patients with single antibodies:\n\n- Four c-negative donors are required for a patient with anti-c.\n- The frequency of the c antigen is 80%.\n- x = 4 / (1 - 0.8) = 20\n- Answer: a minimum of 20 donors should be antigen typed.\n\n*Antigen frequencies forRh C, c, E, e, and D; Kell K and k; Kidd Jk(a) and Jk(b); Duffy Fy(a) and Fy(b); MNS M, N, S, and s; Lewis Le(a) and Le(b); and P1were sourced from the[Laposata’s Laboratory Medicine: Diagnosis of Disease in the Clinical Laboratory, 4th ed.](https://accessmedicine.mhmedical.com/book.aspx?bookid=3574)Frequencies forRh C(w), Kell Kp(a) and Kp(b), and Lutheran Lu(a) and Lu(b)were sourced from the[AABB Technical Manual, 21st ed.](https://www.aabb.org/aabb-store/product/technical-manual-21st-edition---print-16919010)",
  "how_to_use": {
    "why": "An accurate estimate of the number of RBC units to screen helps in the management of blood bank workflow. A prohibitively large estimate of the number of units to screen may require contact outside of the patient’s blood bank (i.e., regional blood donor center, rare blood unit registry).",
    "when": "- À utiliser en contexte de banque de sang pour garantir la compatibilité du receveur avec les RBCs en vue d’une transfusion.\n- Le calculateur est généralement utilisé pour les patients présentant un ou plusieurs allo-anticorps, ou pour les patients à risque de développer des allo-anticorps. Le personnel de laboratoire de banque de sang pourrait trouver ce calculateur particulièrement utile.",
    "pearls": ""
  },
  "next_steps": {
    "advice": "- Follow AABB Standards for respective compatibility testing steps.",
    "critical_actions": "",
    "management": ""
  },
  "evidence": "",
  "more_info": "",
  "short_description": "Donneurs pour le type d'antigène.",
  "medium_description": "Estimates number de donor RBC units pour screen pour obtain desired number de antigen-negative units.",
